{title: Northbound}
{artist: Mara Quinn}

{start_of_verse}
Pack the car before the sun
Leave the key beneath the stone
Every bridge I've ever burned
Lights the way when I'm alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Northbound, northbound
Till the pine trees touch the sky
Northbound, northbound
Never asking why
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Diner coffee, county maps
Radio preacher, static prayers
Every mile a little less
Of the person who was there
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Northbound, northbound
Till the pine trees touch the sky
Northbound, northbound
Never asking why
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
And if you ask me where I'm going
I'll say further than before
And if you ask me what I'm running from
I don't know anymore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse}
Northbound, northbound
Till the pine trees touch the sky
Northbound, northbound
Never asking why
{end_of_verse}
